From: 77450danik <dnsystems@email.ua>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dwmapi: How strongly a backdrop blurs, and windows drawn dark on white.

The Start menus of Windows 10 and 11 in Arctic choose their own blur (the
taskbar's properties, Start menu): DWMWA_ARCTIC_BLUR, 1-100, 0 the default
of dwm.exe. A shell surface over a light backdrop draws dark on white, as
in the light theme: DWMWA_ARCTIC_LIGHT makes dwm.exe key white instead of
black (wine/arctic_dwm.h). Both go into the table dwm.exe shares, as the
accent policy does.
---
 dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c b/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c
--- a/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c
+++ b/dlls/dwmapi/dwmapi_main.c
@@ -189,6 +189,8 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DwmSetWindowAttribute(HWND hwnd, DWORD attributenum, LPCVOID attr
     case 33: /* DWMWA_WINDOW_CORNER_PREFERENCE */
     case 38: /* DWMWA_SYSTEMBACKDROP_TYPE */
     case DWMWA_ARCTIC_TRANSITION:
+    case DWMWA_ARCTIC_BLUR:
+    case DWMWA_ARCTIC_LIGHT:
         if (size < sizeof(DWORD)) return E_INVALIDARG;
         break;
     case DWMWA_ARCTIC_MINIMIZE_RECT:
@@ -215,6 +217,8 @@ HRESULT WINAPI DwmSetWindowAttribute(HWND hwnd, DWORD attributenum, LPCVOID attr
         case 33: window->corner = *(const DWORD *)attribute; break;
         case 38: window->backdrop = *(const DWORD *)attribute; break;
         case DWMWA_ARCTIC_TRANSITION: window->transition = *(const DWORD *)attribute; break;
+        case DWMWA_ARCTIC_BLUR: window->blur = min( *(const DWORD *)attribute, 100 ); break;
+        case DWMWA_ARCTIC_LIGHT: window->light = !!*(const DWORD *)attribute; break;
         case DWMWA_ARCTIC_MINIMIZE_RECT:
         {
             const RECT *rect = attribute;
